## Description of change

1) Structlog was generating lots of logs that looked like this:

```
{"endpoint": "URL('https://dev.court-data-adaptor.service.justice.gov.uk/api/internal/v2/prosecution_cases?filter%5Bname%5D=<PII>&filter%5Bdate_of_birth%5D=<PII>')", "status_code": 200...
```

Resolved this by removing querystrings from any endpoints sent to structlog.

2) Uvicorn's access log was also including querystrings. Resolved this by adding `--no-access-log` and instead adding our own middleware that logs HTTP methods/URLs minus the querystring

3) Outgoing HTTP requests were generating logs from httpx containing PII-containing querystrings. Since we were already manually logging HTTP requests with structlog, resolved this by disabling the redundant httpx logs. 

